    <values>
        <field>Body__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">On January 20, 1992, Cheryl Ann Joe, a young shíshálh mother of three, was found murdered on Powell Street, in Vancouver's Downtown Eastside. That February 14, her mother, Linda Joe, and other women gathered where she was found. Linda Joe wanted the walk to honour every woman who went missing or was killed, not only her daughter. Indigenous women have led it every year since.</value>
